      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.319,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.105,
            0.898,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "61"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.899,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "It is an AP as the difference between the consecutive terms in the list is 80, i.e., d = 80. Also, $a = 8 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.186,
            0.698,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ to find the interest at the end of 30 years, we shall find $a _ { 3 0 ^ { \\circ } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.215,
            0.155,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "Now,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.214,
            0.732,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "a_{30}=a+(30-1)d=80+29\\times80=2400",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.242,
            0.602,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ the interest at the end of 30 years will be \\` 2400."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.275,
            0.902,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "**Example 10 :** In a flower bed, there are 23 rose plants in the first row, 21 in the second, 19 in the third, and so on. There are 5 rose plants in the last row. How many rows are there in the flower bed?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.343,
            0.791,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** The number of rose plants in the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, . . ., rows are :"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.369,
            0.584,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": "2 3 , 2 1 , 1 9 , \\ldots , 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.395,
            0.783,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "It forms an AP (Why?). Let the number of rows in the flower bed be n."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.422,
            0.155,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "Then"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.422,
            0.575,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "a = 23, \\quad d = 21 - 23 = -2, \\quad a_{n} = 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.449,
            0.138,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "As,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.449,
            0.498,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "a_{n} = a + (n - 1)   d",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.474,
            0.194,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "We have,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.475,
            0.531,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "5 = 23 + (n - 1)( - 2)",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.502,
            0.139,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.288,
            0.501,
            0.481,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": "-18 = (n - 1)(-2)",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.528,
            0.139,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.528,
            0.394,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": "n = \\: 1 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_12_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.553,
            0.481,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "So, there are 10 rows in the flower bed."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.573,
            0.368,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": "",
